 {"id":"fabro-528b","title":"fabro_run_create: accept workflow_source-only specs (derive the slug) and reject slug/source mismatch verbosely","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-06T12:26:01.016Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-06T12:26:01.016Z","description":"User design review 2026-09-06 after two consecutive conductor passes burned 6+9 fabro_run_create calls on payload validation: when callers systematically drop required fields, that is a boundary problem (payload validation + verbose errors + contract ergonomics), not a prompt problem. The prompt fixes (56a982d34, 462d033b3) were stopgaps; this seed is the durable fix. Wanted: (1) CreateRunSpec accepts workflow_source-ONLY payloads — the server derives the workflow slug from workflow_source.workflow (it already resolves the source server-side; mx-e21031); (2) when BOTH workflow and workflow_source are present and disagree, reject with an error naming both values (kills the drift class); (3) validation errors name the exact property path and expected shape (overlaps fabro-e4ac — implement together); (4) conductor leg prompts simplify back to the workflow_source-only form once accepted. Rationale: the natural caller payload is valid; redundancy invites drift; every future orchestration agent benefits. Basis: passes 01M1V7Q00XGJ merge@1 (11:30, 6 attempts), 01M1V9DXW8 merge@1 (12:00, 9 attempts), CreateRunSpec.workflow required vs workflow_source optional (create.rs:191-194).","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
 {"id":"fabro-de4d","title":"engine: routing output_schema must constrain preferred_label to the node's outgoing edge labels","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-06T13:22:37.088Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-06T13:22:37.088Z","description":"INCIDENT 2026-09-06, merge-upstream run 01M1V7XSV75BE92JZ0135SHQXK: the reviewer APPROVED (verdict text, merge commit 401e3ceb7 verified) but emitted preferred_label='deploy' — a value no outgoing edge knows. All conditional edges missed, the unconditional soft fallback 'Unrouted review outcome' fired, and the run parked failed(soft_stop) with ~50 min of reviewed merge work stranded on the run branch. output_schema='routing' accepts free-form preferred_label. Wanted: the routing schema validates preferred_label (and any label fields) against the node's outgoing edge labels; on an unknown label, fail the OUTPUT (not the run) with output_retries, error naming the offending value AND the allowed labels — the boundary-first principle (fabro-e4ac class): systematic agent misuse = validation gap, not prompt material. The prompt stopgap (review.md strict routing) landed same day; this seed is the durable fix. Also consider: an unconditional edge without kind should be a graph-validation warning when it is the only unrouted-label catcher (a silent soft park is the most expensive routing failure).","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
 {"id":"fabro-8cd3","title":"web: run status header should render soft_stop (and deadlock/cancelled) distinctly, not plain 'failed'","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-06T13:22:37.212Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-06T14:08:09.175Z","description":"User observation 2026-09-06 on run 01M1V7XSV75BE92JZ0135SHQXK: the status header shows 'failed' although the run parked at a kind=soft exit (reason=soft_stop, work preserved, next pass re-enters autonomously) — indistinguishable at a glance from a hard failure. Wanted: status chip/title renders soft_stop as amber 'soft-stopped' (and deadlock as 'parked — needs human', cancelled distinct from failed), with the failure reason visible without opening the log. ALSO (spec review of fabro-54f0): make failed(approval_timeout) runs visible in the pending/failed list surface — the 54f0 seed's 'surfaced in the UI pending list' requirement was API-side only; this seed owns the web rendering including approval_timeout.","labels":["web","ux"]}
-{"id":"fabro-3d97","title":"engine: automation circuit breaker — pause the schedule after N consecutive identical failure signatures","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-06T13:37:52.532Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-06T13:37:52.532Z","description":"Autonomous-operation gap observed 2026-09-06: three conductor passes parked soft_stop in a row (12:00, 12:30, 13:00 — first a merge routing park, then 2x zai 429 quota exhaustion) and nothing stopped the 30-min cadence. Nothing counts repeated parks; the line happily repeats work or burns sandbox spin-ups all night. Wanted: per-automation consecutive-failure tracking keyed on failure.signature (e.g. api_transient|zai|rate_limited) or (workflow, park-reason); when the SAME signature parks N consecutive automation runs (default e.g. 3), the scheduler pauses the schedule (visible state, like the pause button) and emits ONE aggregated notification (Slack lifecycle exists) naming signature, count, and last run — instead of N single failed-run notifications. A human resumes deliberately; resuming resets the counter. This is the autonomous line's blast-radius limiter for every unknown park cause (routing defects, provider outages, sandbox issues).","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
+{"id":"fabro-3d97","title":"engine: automation circuit breaker — pause the schedule after N consecutive identical failure signatures","status":"in_progress","type":"feature","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-06T13:37:52.532Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-06T18:33:06.025Z","description":"Autonomous-operation gap observed 2026-09-06: three conductor passes parked soft_stop in a row (12:00, 12:30, 13:00 — first a merge routing park, then 2x zai 429 quota exhaustion) and nothing stopped the 30-min cadence. Nothing counts repeated parks; the line happily repeats work or burns sandbox spin-ups all night. Wanted: per-automation consecutive-failure tracking keyed on failure.signature (e.g. api_transient|zai|rate_limited) or (workflow, park-reason); when the SAME signature parks N consecutive automation runs (default e.g. 3), the scheduler pauses the schedule (visible state, like the pause button) and emits ONE aggregated notification (Slack lifecycle exists) naming signature, count, and last run — instead of N single failed-run notifications. A human resumes deliberately; resuming resets the counter. This is the autonomous line's blast-radius limiter for every unknown park cause (routing defects, provider outages, sandbox issues).","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
 {"id":"fabro-1f70","title":"engine: automation honors provider rate-limit reset windows (skip fires until quota reset)","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-06T13:37:52.655Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-06T13:37:52.655Z","description":"Observed 2026-09-06: zai 429 code 1308 'Usage limit reached for 5 hour. Your limit will reset at 2026-09-06 21:11:07' — the reset timestamp rides the raw error body, yet the conductor automation kept firing every 30 min and parking in survey until reset. Cheap (429 fails at open, zero LLM tokens) but pure noise: failed runs, sandbox spin-ups, alert spam. Wanted: when a run parks with a provider rate_limit signature carrying a reset timestamp (parse from detail.raw), the automation scheduler suppresses fires until reset+grace (state visible in the automation); first fire after the window resumes normally. Complements the circuit-breaker seed (this is the KNOWN-cause fast path with an exact ETA).","labels":["engine"]}
 {"id":"fabro-b887","title":"merge-upstream: reuse a parked reviewed merge branch instead of re-merging from scratch","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-06T13:37:52.764Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-06T13:37:52.764Z","description":"Observed 2026-09-06 (run 01M1V7XSV75B): ~50 min of merge+gate+review work (commit 401e3ceb7, reviewer approved all 13 touchpoints) parked on the run branch because the routing label missed (fabro-de4d). The next pass would REDO the entire merge — repeated nightly, each redo burns 40-60 min LLM for identical, already-reviewed output. Wanted (defense in depth beyond de4d): (a) the merge-upstream graph opens the run PR as PART of the approved exit path (before/independent of the final routing), so an approved merge always reaches auto-merge even if later routing parks; and/or (b) the merge stage's prompt starts by checking for an existing parked run branch of the same workflow whose reviewer approved (checkpoint/event evidence) and reuses/promotes that branch (PR) instead of re-merging. Either way: approved work never silently repeats.","labels":["workflows","engine"]}
